    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d569">

                <pb facs="0656" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.248/80: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-11T15:00:00-04:00">May 11, 1940—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>56. Your 103, May 6, 5 p.m. Please again assure the Prime Minister that this
                    Government has given and will continue to give full and sympathetic
                    consideration to his various proposals. However, so far as concerns loans to
                    foreign governments, their agencies and nationals, the only United States
                    Government organization through which loans are made is the Export-Import Bank,
                    which is prevented by the Act of March 2, 1940<anchor n="45a" xml:id="d569-f1"/>
                    from making “any loans for the purchase of any articles, except aircraft
                    exclusively for commercial purposes, listed as arms, ammunition, or implements
                    of war by the President of the United States in accordance with the Neutrality
                    Act of 1939”.<anchor n="45b" xml:id="d569-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Iranian Government is free to make purchases here of military and civil
                    aircraft on the same basis as any other country. The Iranian Aviation Mission
                    has already been placed in touch with manufacturers through the
                    Inter-Departmental Committee and the Department stands ready to arrange further
                    contacts upon request.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
